{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL090aGVyc19MYW5ndWFnZS9GcmVuY2gtTGFuZ3VhZ2UvQ29jbyUyMENoYW5lbCUyMCUyNiUyMElnb3IlMjBTdHJhdmluc2t5JTIwJTI4MjAwOSUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Coco Chanel & Igor Stravinsky","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/gfnBY4gMErWej5afiID9ksTcJPf.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8pa3y1ygj8pCZMNjw3FDfbaI7lI.jpg","description":"Paris 1913. Coco Chanel is infatuated with the rich and handsome Boy Capel, but she is also compelled by her work. Igor Stravinsky's The Rite of Spring is about to be performed. The revolutionary dissonances of Igor's work parallel Coco's radical ideas. She wants to democratize women's fashion; he wants to redefine musical taste. Coco attends the scandalous first performance of The Rite in a chic white dress. The music and ballet are criticized as too modern, too foreign. Coco is moved but Igor is inconsolable.\n\nRated R · Released 24 Sept 2009 · France, Japan · Language: French · 120 min\nStudio: Hexagon Pictures, Eurowide Film Production, Filmazure\n\nOn your server — Audio: French","releaseInfo":"2009","genres":["Drama","Romance","Others"],"imdbRating":"6.1","runtime":"120 min","cast":["Anna Mouglalis","Mads Mikkelsen","Natacha Lindinger","Elena Morozova","Grigori Manoukov","Radivoje Bukvić","Nicolas Vaude","Anatole Taubman"],"director":["Jan Kounen"],"released":"2009-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Jan Kounen","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tAZ5OgqghdubyIwRrViDJVJ4iI.jpg"},{"name":"Anna Mouglalis","character":"Coco Chanel","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/jltxoIc4RbHHUneODrVmawnd8BY.jpg"},{"name":"Mads Mikkelsen","character":"Igor Stravinsky","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/AsX4bdvZ8UCayWTmAf9lAqOA8V7.jpg"},{"name":"Natacha Lindinger","character":"Misia Sert","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/q8gUBeLrS7RolwpNLemOTFl0yUq.jpg"},{"name":"Elena Morozova","character":"Katarina Stravinskaya","